{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Shared.MarkovTraceClaim","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.ofRingHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.ofRingHom","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Shared/ArchimedeanEval.lean#L112-L122","doc":"**The mixin demands nothing beyond a ring hom** — no functoriality, no\nnaturality, no reference to the braided category.\n\nStated as a constructor rather than left implicit, in the manner of\n`TauFunctorTargetSpec.interface_alone_is_trivially_inhabitable`: the reader\nwho sees an `ArchimedeanEval` instance downstream should be able to check,\nmechanically, how little it took to build one. Anything claiming to be the\narchimedean τ-functor has to clear a bar this constructor does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.q_real_one_of_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.q_real_one_of_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Shared/ArchimedeanEval.lean#L99-L110","doc":"**The classical limit now transfers.** `q = 1 → q_real = 1`.\n\nThis is the whole point of the mixin. With `q_real` an independent field it\nwas not provable — `q = 1` constrained nothing about the real parameter, so\na context could sit at the classical value of the substrate parameter and at\nan arbitrary real one simultaneously. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.q_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.q_real","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Shared/ArchimedeanEval.lean#L90-L97","doc":"The real substrate parameter, **derived** as `eval q` rather than posited.\n\nKept under the name the three descendants already used, so every existing\n`ctx.q_real` call site reads identically: dot notation resolves to this\ndefinition exactly as it resolved to the field it replaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.eval","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Shared/ArchimedeanEval.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The archimedean evaluation. **Assumed, not constructed** — see the module\ndocstring. The τ-functor that would supply it with provenance is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Shared/ArchimedeanEval.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.toMarkovTraceContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval.toMarkovTraceContext","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Shared/ArchimedeanEval.lean#L85-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Shared.ArchimedeanEval","kind":"class","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Shared/ArchimedeanEval.lean#L79-L88","doc":"A `MarkovTraceContext` together with an **assumed** archimedean evaluation\n`R →+* ℝ`.\n\nThe ring-homomorphism requirement is what carries the content: it forces\n`eval 1 = 1` and `eval` to respect the ring operations, so `q_real` moves\nwith `q` instead of floating free. ","signatureChunk":0}]}